# The `ape update` verification fixtures are byte-exact: the release signature
# covers the SHA-256 of ape_checksums.txt, and the Sigstore bundle embeds that
# digest. A line-ending conversion (e.g. a Windows autocrlf checkout rewriting
# LF -> CRLF) would change the bytes and break the offline cosign-verify tests.
# Treat them as binary so git never touches their contents.
internal/apecmd/testdata/update/** -text
internal/apecmd/trusted_root.json -text

# Raw PTY output captured from a live Claude Code session. The bytes ARE the
# fixture — "\r\r\n" and relative cursor moves included — and the defect they
# pin was in how those exact bytes render, so a converted copy tests nothing.
internal/repl/testdata/** -text

# APEX's standard ADR-0001, embedded in ape and written into projects byte for
# byte: a project's ADR-0001 is compared with it, and check-framework compares
# it with the framework payload's copy. A CRLF checkout would make every one
# of those differ.
internal/apexv1/standards/** -text
